2021 was a pretty good year for apple  with a lot of awesome product releases  like the new 14 and 16 inch macbook pros  but there were actually a few stones  that apple left unturned as we broke in  the new year and thankfully we're  starting to get some major clues as to  when apple's next event is gonna happen  and what exactly we should be expecting  so what i'm gonna do in this video is  break down the new major apple products  that i fully believe are gonna be coming  at that event as well as the important  details you need to know about those new  products but before we begin let me give  you guys my thoughts on when this event  will take place as we all know apple  hosted their spring event last year in  the month of april but that's only  because the original march date ended up  getting delayed and if you look at  apple's past spring events they almost  always took place in march so april was  an anomaly so in my personal opinion i  believe apple will be holding a march  event this year especially since some of  the products that were supposed to get  released last year in october were  delayed and i think they've been sitting  around just ready to go waiting for the  next event so i think it makes sense for  that event to happen sooner than later  hence the march event now with that said  getting into the products that are  likely to be revealed the first one  we've got to talk about is the mac mini  yes this mac mini has been rumored for  months now and john prosser originally  showed off the leaked design many many  months ago and as you guys can see it's  definitely much thinner it's got a lot  more ports and it has a plexiglass top  for better wireless connectivity now it  was originally supposed to come out last  year alongside the macbook pros at least  according to myself and dylan dkt but  that did not happen because apple  decided to give the macbook pros all of  the spotlight so they had to hold off on  the mac mini and i fully believe that  it's actually been ready for a while  just sitting there waiting for an event  because the redesign justifies an event  reveal and not a regular press release i  also fully believe that it's going to  come packing m1 pro and m1 max chip  options but probably not the new crazy  m1 max duo that a lot of us have been  recently speculating about and we know  this new mac mini is coming for sure  because apple is still selling the  high-end intel mac mini model so this  one is gonna directly replace it and  it's gonna sit above the m1 mac mini and  in terms of the pricing i think it's  going to come at around  12.99 which is actually a good deal  since you're getting the m1 pro chip  compared to paying 2 000  for the 14 inch macbook pro and in terms  of the new second generation m2 mac chip  i don't believe that a mac mini with  that chip is going to be coming until  later this year because i think it's a  low end chip that's going to replace the  m1 mac mini now moving on to the next  product we have the high-end imac now we  obviously know this one is coming  because apple is also still selling the  27-inch intel model on their website and  apple needs to replace it in order to  finish out their two-year apple silicon  transition so i fully guarantee that  this new high-end imac is coming at  apple spring event no doubt about it now  last year dylan dkt was actually the  first one to say that it was getting  delayed until the beginning or the first  half of 2022  and then ross young chimed in and he  more specifically said that it's coming  in the first quarter of 2022 which is  the end of march this is one of the  reasons why i fully believe we're  getting a march event instead of an  april event if ross young's rumor is to  be true now in terms of the design i  expect it to look almost exactly like  the current 24 inch imac just basically  bigger i think it's going to have the  same size chin but the body is going to  be proportionately thicker to allow for  better cooling and more ports and just  to look proportional or good however  this new model is likely to come in a  new space gray color possibly silver but  i'm not sure it all depends on if apple  is going to be calling it the regular  imac  or the imac pro now in terms of the  display size we're almost sure it's  going to be a 27 inch display just like  we had before according to ross young  who has not been wrong yet but he does  believe it's coming with 120 hertz  promotion and mini led technology and  that's going to be likely on at least  one of the models now as far as the chip  and the performance the m1 pro and m1  max chip options are guaranteed but  dylan dkt recently said he believes  there's a good chance that it's gonna  come with at least one more powerful  chip option which i believe is gonna be  the m1 max duo so it's essentially going  to be two m1 max dies connected together  bottom to bottom using special fabric  and i believe this is because the m1 max  die has a totally secret die to die  interconnect section on the bottom which  apple chose to completely edit out of  their dye images and then in terms of  the pricing i fully expect this to start  at around two thousand dollars with the  regular m1 pro chip and it's gonna get  vastly more expensive as you go up to  better chip options now moving on to the  next product that we should expect we  have the new ipad air 5. and this one is  an obvious move by apple because the  current ipad air 4 is grossly outdated  compared to the even cheaper ipad mini 6  since the current air still has the a14  chip compared to the a15 and the mini so  it makes no sense at all in the lineup  and because of that i can 100 guarantee  that it's going to be coming this spring  but i'm not exactly sure if it's going  to show up at the event or if it's just  going to be a press release now just the  other day apple actually registered  multiple model numbers with the eec  which means that we should expect this  new ipad to come soon for sure but in  terms of the upgrade i believe it's  going to be very boring i think it's  going to have the same price as before  but it's just gonna get updated to match  some of the specs of the ipad mini 6 but  with some extra upgrades we should be  expecting the new 12 megapixel ultra  wide selfie camera with center stage  support we should expect the a15 chip  optional 5g cellular connectivity quad  led true tone flash and maybe even quad  stereo speakers and an ipad pro like  dual camera system on the back and now  with that said we finally have the new  iphone se3 which has been rumored for  many months now and unfortunately this  is also going to be a very minor upgrade  instead of the awesome 6.1 inch display  that was rumored in the past it's not  going to be getting a redesign at all  and it's going to be sticking with the  same 4.7 inch display design as before  which does include the home button and  as far as the new features it's simply  going to get a spec update with a new  chip most likely the a15 chip 5g  cellular connectivity and that's  probably it and in my opinion i think  the price is going to stay at the exact  same 399  which is going to make it a big deal for  emerging markets like india now as far  as this new iphone i think there's a  pretty good chance that it's actually  going to be released with a press  release instead of being shown off at  the spring event because it is such a  boring update and we did get some leaks  from leaks apple pro which showed that  apple may have delayed it until april so  it'll be perfect for a press release but  other than that there's a chance we'll  be getting some other new products maybe  like a new iphone 13 color or maybe just  some updates to some of apple's less  popular accessories or products but we  don't really know because we don't have  any rumors in terms of those products  but there you guys go if you're excited  for apple's upcoming event then go ahead  and click the circle abov